ated AppConfig.java (@Configuration, @ComponentScan, @PropertySource), DatabaseConfig.java (DBCP2 DataSource, SqlSessionFactoryBean with type aliases + mapper locations, DataSourceTransactionManager, static MapperScannerConfigurer), WebConfig.java (@EnableWebMvc, Jackson ObjectMapper with local TZ, CORS), WebInitializer.java (AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer), application.properties (PostgreSQL defaults).\nWhy: MapperScannerConfigurer is a BeanDefinitionRegistryPostProcessor that runs before @Value properties are resolved — declared static @Bean to avoid premature injection failures. ObjectMapper configured with setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) per LEARNINGS.md for correct @JsonFormat behavior.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Static @Bean pattern for MapperScannerConfigurer is the standard mitigation for BDRPP ordering issue.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:06:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 5 - Security configuration\nChanges: Created SecurityConfig.java (@EnableWebSecurity, extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter) with HTTP Basic auth, stateless sessions, CSRF disabled, in-memory users (admin/admin123 ADMIN, user/user123 USER), role-based URL patterns (GET requires USER|ADMIN, POST/PUT/DELETE requires ADMIN), custom AuthenticationEntryPoint (401 JSON) and AccessDeniedHandler (403 JSON). Created SecurityWebApplicationInitializer.java (extends AbstractSecurityWebApplicationInitializer) to register DelegatingFilterProxy. Updated WebInitializer.getRootConfigClasses() to include SecurityConfig.\nWhy: AbstractSecurityWebApplicationInitializer is required for Java-config (no web.xml) to register the springSecurityFilterChain filter. SecurityConfig must be in the root context (not servlet context) so it applies to all requests before dispatch. Custom entry points return JSON ErrorResponse instead of default Spring Security HTML/Basic-challenge responses.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Spring Security 4.2 in-memory auth with plain text passwords works without {noop} prefix (that prefix is Spring Security 5+).\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:15:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 6 - EmployeeMapper interface and MyBatis XML\nChanges: Created EmployeeMapper.java interface in com.example.legacy.mapper with 9 methods (findAll, findById, insert, update, delete, countAll, searchByNameOrDepartment, countBySearch, findByEmail). @Param annotations on all multi-param methods. Created src/main/resources/mappers/EmployeeMapper.xml with resultMap for snake_case→camelCase column mapping and all 9 SQL statements. Search uses <choose> dynamic SQL for OR logic: both params → (name LIKE OR dept LIKE), one param → LIKE on that param only. Case-insensitive via LOWER(). INSERT uses useGeneratedKeys=\"true\" keyProperty=\"id\". UPDATE explicitly sets updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.\nWhy: resultMap needed because DB columns are snake_case (hire_date, created_at, updated_at) while Java fields are camelCase and mapUnderscoreToCamelCase is not enabled in config. <choose> for search avoids malformed SQL when one param is null (service enforces at-least-one-non-null invariant). CURRENT_TIMESTAMP used instead of NOW() for H2 compatibility in tests.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:20:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 7 - EmployeeValidator\nChanges: Created com.example.legacy.exception package with DuplicateEmailException, NotFoundException, BadRequestException. Created com.example.legacy.validation.EmployeeValidator (@Component) with validateCreate(email) and validateUpdate(currentId, email) methods. validateCreate throws DuplicateEmailException if email already exists; validateUpdate throws only if email belongs to a different employee (id mismatch).\nWhy: Created all three exception classes now (not just DuplicateEmailException) because NotFoundException and BadRequestException are small, needed by Item 9 (service) and Item 10 (exception handler), and creating them now avoids a separate session for trivial boilerplate. EmployeeValidator takes EmployeeMapper via constructor injection for testability.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:30:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 8 - Test infrastructure\nChanges: Created TestAppConfig.java in src/test/java/com/example/legacy/config/ — standalone H2 config with DataSource (MODE=PostgreSQL), DataSourceInitializer (runs test schema.sql on context load), SqlSessionFactoryBean (same mapper XML path as production), DataSourceTransactionManager, and static MapperScannerConfigurer. Created BaseIntegrationTest.java in src/test/java/com/example/legacy/support/ — abstract base with @RunWith(SpringJUnit4ClassRunner.class), @ContextConfiguration(TestAppConfig.class), @Transactional for automatic per-test transaction rollback.\nWhy: TestAppConfig is self-contained (no @ComponentScan, no property injection) to avoid conflicting with production DatabaseConfig/AppConfig beans. H2 in-memory DB with MODE=PostgreSQL and DROP TABLE IF EXISTS in schema.sql ensures clean state on every context load. @Transactional on BaseIntegrationTest rolls back data changes after each test method without needing explicit cleanup. DataSourceInitializer is the standard Spring 4.x mechanism for running schema scripts against an arbitrary DataSource.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. All existing tests continue to pass.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
