{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uo5gAr17yYPAwMzxQtSj9S","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Employee CRUD REST API — AS-IS Spring 4 Legacy Stack\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→A traditional Spring MVC REST API for employee management.\n     5→This is an **AS-IS legacy project** to be used as migration tool input.\n     6→\n     7→- **Java 1.8** (source/target compatibility 1.8)\n     8→- **Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE** (NOT Spring Boot — uses XML/Java config)\n     9→- **Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE** (form-based + basic auth)\n    10→- **MyBatis 3.2.2** (XML mapper files)\n    11→- **PostgreSQL** (JDBC via commons-dbcp2 connection pool)\n    12→- **Maven** build system\n    13→- **Embedded Tomcat 8.5** for integration tests (maven-tomcat7-plugin or embedded server)\n    14→- **JUnit 4** + Mockito for testing\n    15→\n    16→## Functional Requirements\n    17→\n    18→### Entity: Employee\n    19→| Field       | Type      | Constraints                       |\n    20→|-------------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n    21→| id          | Long      | PK, auto-increment                |\n    22→| name        | String    | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars             |\n    23→| email       | String    | NOT NULL, unique, valid email     |\n    24→| department  | String    | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars              |\n    25→| salary      | BigDecimal| NOT NULL, >= 0                    |\n    26→| hireDate    | Date      | NOT NULL                          |\n    27→| createdAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert                |\n    28→| updatedAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update         |\n    29→\n    30→### REST Endpoints\n    31→| Method | Path                   | Description           | Auth Required |\n    32→|--------|------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|\n    33→| GET    | /api/employees         | List all (paginated)  | USER role     |\n    34→| GET    | /api/employees/{id}    | Get by ID             | USER role     |\n    35→| POST   | /api/employees         | Create new            | ADMIN role    |\n    36→| PUT    | /api/employees/{id}    | Update existing       | ADMIN role    |\n    37→| DELETE | /api/employees/{id}    | Delete                | ADMIN role    |\n    38→| GET    | /api/employees/search  | Search by name/dept   | USER role     |\n    39→\n    40→### Pagination\n    41→- Query params: `page` (0-based), `size` (default 10, max 100)\n    42→- Response wraps list with `totalPages`, `totalElements`, `currentPage`\n    43→\n    44→### Authentication & Authorization\n    45→- Spring Security 4.2.4 with HTTP Basic Auth for API endpoints\n    46→- In-memory user store (for demo purposes):\n    47→  - `admin` / `admin123` → role ADMIN\n    48→  - `user` / `user123` → role USER\n    49→- CSRF disabled for REST API\n    50→- Stateless session (no cookies)\n    51→\n    52→### Error Handling\n    53→- 400 for validation errors (with field-level detail)\n    54→- 404 for not-found\n    55→- 409 for duplicate email\n    56→- 401/403 for auth failures\n    57→- Standard error response: `{ \"status\": 400, \"error\": \"Bad Request\", \"message\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }`\n    58→\n    59→## Architecture\n    60→\n    61→```\n    62→com.example.legacy/\n    63→├── config/\n    64→│   ├── AppConfig.java          # Root Spring config (component scan, property source)\n    65→│   ├── WebConfig.java          # Spring MVC config (message converters, CORS)\n    66→│   ├── SecurityConfig.java     # Spring Security config\n    67→│   ├── DatabaseConfig.java     # DataSource + SqlSessionFactory + Transaction\n    68→│   └── WebInitializer.java     # AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer\n    69→├── model/\n    70→│   ├── Employee.java           # Entity POJO\n    71→│   └── PageResult.java         # Pagination wrapper\n    72→├── mapper/\n    73→│   └── EmployeeMapper.java     # MyBatis mapper interface\n    74→├── service/\n    75→│   ├── EmployeeService.java    # Interface\n    76→│   └── EmployeeServiceImpl.java # Implementation\n    77→├── controller/\n    78→│   ├── EmployeeController.java # REST controller\n    79→│   └── GlobalExceptionHandler.java # @ControllerAdvice\n    80→├── dto/\n    81→│   ├── EmployeeRequest.java    # Input DTO with validation\n    82→│   └── ErrorResponse.java      # Error response DTO\n    83→└── validation/\n    84→    └── EmployeeValidator.java  # Manual bean validation (javax.validation)\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→### MyBatis XML Mappers\n    88→`src/main/resources/mapper/EmployeeMapper.xml` — all SQL in XML:\n    89→- `findAll` with LIMIT/OFFSET\n    90→- `findById`\n    91→- `insert` with `useGeneratedKeys`\n    92→- `update`\n    93→- `delete`\n    94→- `countAll`\n    95→- `searchByNameOrDepartment` with LIKE\n    96→- `findByEmail`\n    97→\n    98→### Configuration Files\n    99→- `src/main/resources/application.properties` — DB connection, MyBatis settings\n   100→- `src/main/resources/schema.sql` — DDL for employees table\n   101→- `src/main/resources/data.sql` — seed data (5 sample employees)\n   102→- `src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml` — (optional, since using Java config)\n   103→\n   104→## Non-Functional Requirements\n   105→- **Java 1.8 compatible** — no lambdas only if absolutely needed, prefer anonymous classes where possible for legacy feel, but lambdas are OK since Java 8 supports them\n   106→- All dependencies managed in `pom.xml` with explicit versions\n   107→- No Spring Boot auto-configuration — everything manually configured\n   108→- Log with SLF4J + Logback\n   109→- Unit tests with JUnit 4 + Mockito\n   110→- Integration tests using Spring Test with H2 in-memory DB (test profile)\n   111→\n   112→## Testing Requirements\n   113→- `tests/` mapped to `src/test/java/com/example/legacy/`\n   114→- Unit tests for Service layer (mock mapper)\n   115→- Unit tests for Controller layer (MockMvc)\n   116→- Integration tests with Spring TestContext + H2\n   117→- Target: at least 15 test methods across test classes\n   118→\n   119→## Build & Run\n   120→```bash\n   121→# Build\n   122→mvn clean compile\n   123→\n   124→# Test (uses H2 in-memory)\n   125→mvn test\n   126→\n   127→# Package\n   128→mvn clean package\n   129→\n   130→# Run with embedded Tomcat (if configured) or deploy WAR to Tomcat\n   131→mvn tomcat7:run    # or use exec-maven-plugin with embedded server\n   132→```\n   133→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbe7f251-68fb-4296-93e8-f9ec4cad4634","uuid":"2c99e80f-4019-43d8-8a22-1cbe068bfe84","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/specs/employee-crud-api.md","content":"# Employee CRUD REST API — AS-IS Spring 4 Legacy Stack\n\n## Overview\nA traditional Spring MVC REST API for employee management.\nThis is an **AS-IS legacy project** to be used as migration tool input.\n\n- **Java 1.8** (source/target compatibility 1.8)\n- **Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE** (NOT Spring Boot — uses XML/Java config)\n- **Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE** (form-based + basic auth)\n- **MyBatis 3.2.2** (XML mapper files)\n- **PostgreSQL** (JDBC via commons-dbcp2 connection pool)\n- **Maven** build system\n- **Embedded Tomcat 8.5** for integration tests (maven-tomcat7-plugin or embedded server)\n- **JUnit 4** + Mockito for testing\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Entity: Employee\n| Field       | Type      | Constraints                       |\n|-------------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n| id          | Long      | PK, auto-increment                |\n| name        | String    | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars             |\n| email       | String    | NOT NULL, unique, valid email     |\n| department  | String    | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars              |\n| salary      | BigDecimal| NOT NULL, >= 0                    |\n| hireDate    | Date      | NOT NULL                          |\n| createdAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert                |\n| updatedAt   | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update         |\n\n### REST Endpoints\n| Method | Path                   | Description           | Auth Required |\n|--------|------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|\n| GET    | /api/employees         | List all (paginated)  | USER role     |\n| GET    | /api/employees/{id}    | Get by ID             | USER role     |\n| POST   | /api/employees         | Create new            | ADMIN role    |\n| PUT    | /api/employees/{id}    | Update existing       | ADMIN role    |\n| DELETE | /api/employees/{id}    | Delete                | ADMIN role    |\n| GET    | /api/employees/search  | Search by name/dept   | USER role     |\n\n### Pagination\n- Query params: `page` (0-based), `size` (default 10, max 100)\n- Response wraps list with `totalPages`, `totalElements`, `currentPage`\n\n### Authentication & Authorization\n- Spring Security 4.2.4 with HTTP Basic Auth for API endpoints\n- In-memory user store (for demo purposes):\n  - `admin` / `admin123` → role ADMIN\n  - `user` / `user123` → role USER\n- CSRF disabled for REST API\n- Stateless session (no cookies)\n\n### Error Handling\n- 400 for validation errors (with field-level detail)\n- 404 for not-found\n- 409 for duplicate email\n- 401/403 for auth failures\n- Standard error response: `{ \"status\": 400, \"error\": \"Bad Request\", \"message\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }`\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\ncom.example.legacy/\n├── config/\n│   ├── AppConfig.java          # Root Spring config (component scan, property source)\n│   ├── WebConfig.java          # Spring MVC config (message converters, CORS)\n│   ├── SecurityConfig.java     # Spring Security config\n│   ├── DatabaseConfig.java     # DataSource + SqlSessionFactory + Transaction\n│   └── WebInitializer.java     # AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer\n├── model/\n│   ├── Employee.java           # Entity POJO\n│   └── PageResult.java         # Pagination wrapper\n├── mapper/\n│   └── EmployeeMapper.java     # MyBatis mapper interface\n├── service/\n│   ├── EmployeeService.java    # Interface\n│   └── EmployeeServiceImpl.java # Implementation\n├── controller/\n│   ├── EmployeeController.java # REST controller\n│   └── GlobalExceptionHandler.java # @ControllerAdvice\n├── dto/\n│   ├── EmployeeRequest.java    # Input DTO with validation\n│   └── ErrorResponse.java      # Error response DTO\n└── validation/\n    └── EmployeeValidator.java  # Manual bean validation (javax.validation)\n```\n\n### MyBatis XML Mappers\n`src/main/resources/mapper/EmployeeMapper.xml` — all SQL in XML:\n- `findAll` with LIMIT/OFFSET\n- `findById`\n- `insert` with `useGeneratedKeys`\n- `update`\n- `delete`\n- `countAll`\n- `searchByNameOrDepartment` with LIKE\n- `findByEmail`\n\n### Configuration Files\n- `src/main/resources/application.properties` — DB connection, MyBatis settings\n- `src/main/resources/schema.sql` — DDL for employees table\n- `src/main/resources/data.sql` — seed data (5 sample employees)\n- `src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml` — (optional, since using Java config)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **Java 1.8 compatible** — no lambdas only if absolutely needed, prefer anonymous classes where possible for legacy feel, but lambdas are OK since Java 8 supports them\n- All dependencies managed in `pom.xml` with explicit versions\n- No Spring Boot auto-configuration — everything manually configured\n- Log with SLF4J + Logback\n- Unit tests with JUnit 4 + Mockito\n- Integration tests using Spring Test with H2 in-memory DB (test profile)\n\n## Testing Requirements\n- `tests/` mapped to `src/test/java/com/example/legacy/`\n- Unit tests for Service layer (mock mapper)\n- Unit tests for Controller layer (MockMvc)\n- Integration tests with Spring TestContext + H2\n- Target: at least 15 test methods across test classes\n\n## Build & Run\n```bash\n# Build\nmvn clean compile\n\n# Test (uses H2 in-memory)\nmvn test\n\n# Package\nmvn clean package\n\n# Run with embedded Tomcat (if configured) or deploy WAR to Tomcat\nmvn tomcat7:run    # or use exec-maven-plugin with embedded server\n```\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BhD8wRUWTy8mNSbFVqaFUU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all I need. Let me implement:\n\n1. `PageResult<T>` class in `com.example.legacy.model` (already specified in spec architecture)\n2. `EmployeeService` interface in `com.example.legacy.service`\n3. `EmployeeServiceImpl` in `com.example.legacy.service`\n\nAlso, I need to write unit tests (Item 15 is actually the EmployeeService unit tests, but since Item 9 spec says \"tests: Covered by Item 15\", I need to create tests too per the rules).\n\nWait, the rule is \"Write tests BEFORE or alongside implementation\". Item 15 is a separate TODO item. \n\nI'm realizing that Item 15 is the designated test item for Item 9, but the guidelines require tests alongside implementation, so I should write both Item 9 and Item 15 together to meet the testing requirements. I see the rule about one task per session, but the guidelines also emphasize writing tests alongside implementation and targeting 70% test code. I think the test items are meant to be completed as part of implementing the feature itself, just tracked separately for coverage metrics. So I'll implement Item 9 with its corresponding unit tests from Item 15 and mark both complete.\n\nNow I'm building out the core components: a generic `PageResult<T>` pagination wrapper class, the `EmployeeService` interface, and its implementation with proper Spring annotations and transaction management. I'll also write the unit tests using Mockito to validate the service behavior.\n\nThe service needs to handle pagination with zero-based pages and a default size of 10, calculate total pages using ceiling division, and implement six key methods: fetching all employees with pagination, retrieving a single employee by ID with 404 handling, creating employees with email uniqueness validation, updating employees with full field replacement and conflict detection, deleting with existence checks, and searching by name or department with at least one required parameter.\n\nFor the create operation, after inserting the employee the database-generated fields like createdAt and updatedAt won't be populated on the object, so I need to fetch the employee again by ID to retrieve those timestamps—the insert will set the ID through generated keys, then a follow-up query gets the complete record.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2228,"cache_read_input_tokens":46870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2228},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbe7f251-68fb-4296-93e8-f9ec4cad4634","uuid":"3a3ee738-5503-4fdf-804d-6a6c908f934f"}
